   772	// current-device query's error. Now every record carries WHICH CUDA call failed and FOR WHAT, with the device that call
   773	// concerned and its error: a plain-data tag of two bytes, so recording stays a copy of a few words (allocation-free,
   774	// noexcept, saturating: V6-03) and `merge` keeps the tags. Every message is built from the tag (describe() below): it
   775	// names the failed CUDA call and its device, and never an operation that succeeded.
