  1606	void drain_completed() noexcept {
  1607	  PendingState& st = pending();
  1608	  while (!st.q.empty()) {
  1609	    const cudaError_t r = test_hooks::take(test_hooks::kCudaEventQuery) ? kTestInjectedCudaError
  1610	                                                                          : cudaEventQuery(st.q.front().event);
  1611	    if (r != cudaSuccess) {
  1612	      // cudaErrorNotReady: still pending (FIFO: later entries wait too). CUDA 12.6 does not leave NotReady in the
  1613	      // last-error slot (ledger receipt; Programming Guide 3.2.12: NotReady "is not considered an error"); clear it
  1614	      // defensively if a runtime ever does. Any other error (a broken context) leaves the entry for
  1615	      // synchronize_and_release_all, which re-queries it and reports and leaks it if the device cannot synchronize.
  1616	      // P1T-FIX4 (sweep): that other error's slot entry is consumed here (62c8d9f left it, so the next, unrelated
  1617	      // launch check reported it as its own); the entry itself still carries the failure to synchronize().
  1618	      // P1T-FIX5, round-5 review finding V5-02 (MINOR): FIX4's last clause was wrong for a ONE-SHOT failure. The entry
  1619	      // stays queued, but a queued entry does not remember the error: synchronize() re-queries it, and if the query now
  1620	      // succeeds the entry is released and synchronize() returns success, so the failure was consumed and never
  1621	      // reported (review probe query_error_cpu.py / query_error_single_gpu.py; FIX4 sweep rows 47 and 50). Now a
  1622	      // non-NotReady failure is RECORDED first (counted in event_query_failures and noted as a failure where nothing
  1623	      // can raise: the drain is noexcept and runs at the start of an unrelated call), and only then is the slot entry
  1624	      // consumed; the next synchronize() raises it exactly once (FIX4's deferred-error routing, cleared once its message
  1625	      // exists). Completion and release stay as before: the entry is left for synchronize(), which re-queries it and
  1626	      // releases on a successful query, or leaks it with no completion proof. NotReady is not recorded: CUDA 12.6
