  1292	const char* const kDlpackDoc = R"doc(Export this tensor zero-copy as a DLPack capsule (Python array API protocol).
  1293	
  1294	stream: the CONSUMER's CUDA stream, as a DLPack int. TensorCUDA queues all of its
  1295	  work on the legacy default stream.
  1296	  * None or 1: the consumer is on the legacy default stream; nothing to do.
  1297	  * -1: no synchronization.
  1298	  * 2 (per-thread default stream) or any other handle (a cudaStream_t): TensorCUDA
  1299	    records a CUDA event on the legacy default stream of THIS TENSOR'S device and
  1300	    makes the consumer's stream wait on it before returning, so the consumer sees
  1301	    every TensorCUDA write queued so far. If another device is current, TensorCUDA
  1302	    switches to the tensor's device for the fence and restores the caller's device
  1303	    (also when the fence fails, before raising RuntimeError). With 2, the wait is
  1304	    on the per-thread default stream of the tensor's device; a handle may belong
  1305	    to any device (a cross-device event wait is legal in CUDA).
  1306	  * 0 is ambiguous under the protocol and raises ValueError.
  1307	Device proof (P1T-FIX4): before anything else, the tensor's device label is
  1308	checked against its allocation (cudaPointerGetAttributes); a tensor whose memory
  1309	is on another device than its label (the engine labels its own allocations
  1310	cuda:0, so one allocated while another device was current) raises BufferError.
  1311	max_version: None (or major < 1) returns a legacy "dltensor" capsule; (1, x) or
  1312	  later returns "dltensor_versioned" (DLPack 1.3 header, flags 0).
  1313	dl_device: None or (2, this tensor's device); anything else raises BufferError.
  1314	copy: None or False. copy=True raises BufferError (TensorCUDA never copies on
  1315	  export).
  1316	
  1317	The capsule's manager holds a reference to the tensor's Storage, so the memory
  1318	outlives this Tensor's last Python reference. data + byte_offset addresses
  1319	element 0; strides are C-contiguous. An unconsumed capsule releases its
  1320	reference when it is garbage collected.
  1321	
  1322	Raises BufferError for CPU tensors.
  1323	
  1324	External in-place writes (mark_modified rule): TensorCUDA's derived-tensor
  1325	caches key on the Storage revision, which only TensorCUDA's own in-place ops
  1326	bump. After anything outside TensorCUDA (a DLPack consumer, or a kernel given
  1327	data_ptr()) writes into this tensor's memory, call t.mark_modified() before
  1328	passing t (or any tensor sharing its Storage) to a TensorCUDA op. Today the
  1329	only revision-keyed cache is terrain_render's density_filter cache on the
  1330	materials tensor; ops that read device memory directly (arithmetic, matmul,
  1331	norms, attention) need nothing. Calling mark_modified() when it is not needed
  1332	is harmless.)doc";
