  1334	// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ P1T-FIX6 sweep (g)
  1335	// User Python run from inside a native frame. pybind11's typed argument casters convert in the dispatcher, before the
  1336	// function body (an int parameter calls __index__, a double __float__ / __index__, a std::vector __len__ /
  1337	// __getitem__ and each item's conversion), its no-match TypeError calls repr() on every argument, and its keyword
  1338	// matching uses dict lookups that may call a str subclass's __eq__. Any of that user Python can release the GIL on a
  1339	// daemon thread across the start of finalization; CPython 3.12 then exits the thread when it re-takes the GIL and the
  1340	// forced unwind runs the dispatcher's C++ cleanup (its private kwargs copy is deallocated with the thread's state
  1341	// freed: `_C.empty(shape=SeqLen())` rc 139 2/2 on acd42fa, ledger 07:32-07:40). Every P1-T binding of this module is
  1342	// therefore declared as (*args, **kwargs) -- for that signature the dispatcher copies, converts and looks up nothing
  1343	// and cannot mismatch (a method's self arrives as args[0]) -- and CoreCallArgs below matches positions and keyword
  1344	// names with C-level comparisons (PyUnicode_CompareWithASCIIString reads the string data, also for a str subclass);
  1345	// the converters accept exactly the types whose value is read without calling a Python method (int and subclasses via
  1346	// PyLong_AsLongLongAndOverflow; float and subclasses via PyFloat_AsDouble; tuple / list via the C macros; str via
  1347	// PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize; bytes via PyBytes_AS_STRING) and refuse everything else with TypeError naming the type.
  1348	// Same design as the add-on's tc_signal/src/py_args.h (a copy: core includes nothing from the add-on, and this order
  1349	// adds no core file). Prior art: CPython's C argument parser (Python/getargs.c: keyword matching without __eq__;
  1350	// unverified, lead to check "getargs.c find_keyword"); PyTorch 2.11 Tensor.__dlpack__'s `type(stream) is not int`
  1351	// refusal (installed torch/_tensor.py); pybind11's py::args / py::kwargs. Ours: applying it to every P1-T binding.
  1352	struct CoreParam {
  1353	  const char* name;
  1354	  bool required = true;
  1355	};
