   400	// while an earlier report was being raised and is therefore not named), and their consumption by the raise. The count
   401	// is atomic (a Storage may die on any thread); the named first one is kept under the record's mutex. Prior art: the
   402	// add-on's N1 / V6-03 raise-once records (tc_signal dlpack_operand.cpp); no specific external prior art known to me.
   403	void dlpack_unreported_unraisable(unsigned long long* count, std::string* what, int* device, int* error) {
   404	  CoreUnraisableRecord& r = core_unraisable_record();
   405	  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(r.mu);
   406	  *count = g_core_unraisable_unreported.load();
